the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the property assessment of the situation is *a number*.
    the previous year property assessment of the situation is *a number*.
    the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is *a number*.
    the one year percent of the parameters is *a number*.
    the five year percent of the parameters is *a number*.
    the check result is *a truth value*.
    the one year increase of the check result is *a truth value*.
    the five year increase of the check result is *a truth value*.

the knowledge base property_assessment_increase includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/property-assessment-increase.dmn".

rule check_result_1 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the one year increase of the check result is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the previous year property assessment of the situation is a third number
                or it is not the case that the one year percent of the parameters is a fifth number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number P
    and the one year percent of the parameters is a number Q
    and K >= P * (1 + Q / 100).

rule check_result_2 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the one year increase of the check result is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the previous year property assessment of the situation is a third number
                or it is not the case that the one year percent of the parameters is a fifth number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number P
    and the one year percent of the parameters is a number Q
    and K < P * (1 + Q / 100).

rule check_result_3 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the five year increase of the check result is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a third number
                or it is not the case that the five year percent of the parameters is a fifth number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number P
    and the five year percent of the parameters is a number Q
    and K >= P * (1 + Q / 100).

rule check_result_4 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the five year increase of the check result is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a third number
                or it is not the case that the five year percent of the parameters is a fifth number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number P
    and the five year percent of the parameters is a number Q
    and K < P * (1 + Q / 100).

rule check_result_5 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is true if
    the one year increase of the check result is true.

rule check_result_6 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is true if
    the five year increase of the check result is true.

rule check_result_7 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is false if
    the one year increase of the check result is false
    and the five year increase of the check result is false.

